-.117(ABCRATE)A
f0_12 sf
-.088( is a computer program for the calculation of atom-diatom chemical)A
72 330 :M
-.115(reaction rates for systems with collinear-dominated dynamics.  The dynamical methods)A
72 348 :M
-.128(used are conventional or generalized transition state theory \(GTST\) and multidimensional)A
72 366 :M
-.108(semiclassical approximations for tunneling and nonclassical reflection.  The GTST methods)A
72 384 :M
-.136(included in this version of the program are canonical and improved canonical variational)A
72 402 :M
-.121(transition state theory \(VTST\) and the canonical unified statistical \(CUS\) method.  Rate)A
72 420 :M
-.126(constants may be calculated for canonical ensembles or for specific vibrational states of)A
72 438 :M
-.114(selected modes with translational, rotational, and other vibrational modes treated thermally.)A
72 456 :M
-.125(The potential energy surface required by the program may be a global or semiglobal)A
72 474 :M
-.122(analytic function.  The reaction path is calculated as the path of steepest descent in mass-)A
72 492 :M
-.109(scaled coordinates from a collinear saddle point, and vibrations transverse to the reaction)A
72 510 :M
-.124(path are treated by curvilinear internal coordinates.  The vibrational modes are quantized,)A
72 528 :M
-.102(and anharmonicity may be included by various options, including the WKB approximation)A
72 546 :M
-.114(for bond stretches and the centrifugal oscillator approximation through quartic terms for the)A
72 564 :M
-.134(curvilinear bend coordinate.  Tunneling probabilities are calculated by a variety of)A
72 582 :M
-.114(semiclassical methods, in particular zero-curvature tunneling \(ZCT\), small-curvature)A
72 600 :M
-.099(tunneling \(SCT\), large-curvature tunneling \(LCT\), least-action tunneling \(LAT\), and the)A
72 617 :M
-.15(microcanonical optimized multidimensional tunneling \()A
f1_12 sf
-.206(m)A
f0_12 sf
-.192(OMT\) methods.)A
72 646 :M
