72 231 :M
-.057(\(The first four of these methods are usually abbreviated ZCT, SCT, LCT, and LAT,)A
72 255 :M
-.087(respectively.\)  The program can also be used to carry out stationary point analyses for)A
72 279 :M
-.1(transition states and conventional transition state theory rate constants.  First the program)A
72 303 :M
-.133(optimizes the geometry of the reactant diatomic, the product diatomic, and the saddle)A
72 327 :M
-.061(point\(s\) \(if any exist\).  The program is designed to handle zero to four saddle points.  The)A
72 351 :M
-.097(reference path is found by following the path of steepest descent in a mass-scaled)A
72 375 :M
-.118(coordinate system from a collinear saddle point or from a pre-specified point in the)A
72 399 :M
-.126(asymptotic region \(the latter option is for exoergic reactions with monotonically downhill)A
72 423 :M
-.148(reaction paths\).  Tunneling probabilities are calculated analytically by the Wigner method)A
72 447 :M
-.121(and semiclassically \(six methods listed above\) by numerical quadrature.  The variational)A
72 471 :M
-.147(transition state of canonical variational theory and improved canonical variational theory is)A
72 495 :M
